    "title": "feat(call-me): wire contract (v0.2) + zero-dep CLI to ring the owner from any shell",
    "body": "**Draft — behind the sprint pin; proposal for warden's lane-pick (per bundle, respawn 0a0d1325). Two-key via @claude-warden.**\n\nCarter's ask: a `call-me` command available **from anywhere** — a microVM, a vscode terminal, CI, or wrapped as an MCP tool so non-Claude agents can fire it. This adds the wire contract + the CLI.\n\n## What\n- **`docs/CALL_ME_AND_VOICE_CONTRACT.md` (v0.2)** — the ONE wire contract that keeps machine (transport) and forge (voice layer + CLI) from colliding, per bundle's seam ruling. **Grounded in the live gateway** (`services/pocket-gateway/API.md` + `src/need-carter-dial.mjs` + `src/handlers.mjs`), not invented.\n- **`tools/call-me/call-me.mjs`** — a zero-dependency Node client over `POST /dial/ring-owner`.\n- **`tools/call-me/call-me.test.mjs`** — 14 `node:test` cases, all green.\n\n## Security (server-enforced; the client cannot bypass)\n- **Confused-deputy-safe both ways:** the human **target** and the caller **identity** are derived server-side from the token, never the body. A token holder cannot redirect the ring, nor ring *as* someone else (AMEND-2).\n- **No provider keys in a box:** the CLI holds only a scoped, short-TTL `pocket:dial` token (`SENTI_DIAL_TOKEN`); the voice-provider key stays server-side behind `/tts`.\n- **Doorbell backoff (AMEND-1):** honors `Retry-After` on 429, bounded retries on 429/503/network with one stable idempotency key (exactly-once per ring), then non-zero exit — a looping box can never ring-spam Carter's phone.\n\n## Shape review status\n- Contract **shape-gated CLOSED by @respawn-bundle** (all v0.2 amendments folded).\n- **Open:** @respawn-machine still owes the **transport-half confirmation** — the two new server-side surfaces are machine's: the per-token/per-session **429 rate limiter** and the **server-stamped caller identity**. Plus v0.3 ANSWER-path ownership (declared out-of-scope here).\n\n## Release gates (unchanged, machine/warden)\nRoute stays dark until sentinelayer-api **#783** (membership) is deployed/smoke-proven; APNs off by default; physical-device evidence.\n\n## Verification\n`node --test` → **14/14 green**; `--dry-run` builds the correct request; `pickOption` atomic with its options; network failure → bounded retry → non-zero exit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
